// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/automation/service_ledger.t27 -- ONE principle for every service this project
// sells: a service never holds, prices or moves money; it emits a receipt, one splitter
// reads that receipt, and the distribution is decided by rules alone -- so no person sits
// in the path of a payment, no payment exists without a receipt, and no balance exists
// without an entry that a receipt wrote.
// Trace: owner, 2026-10-23: "all the courses are open, and their creators are paid $TRI
//       for them; I am the first creator of them", and the same day "one principle for
//       every service, and all the accounting and the distribution of money is settled
//       without any person taking part".
// The services this one rule covers (SERVICES): a course a person publishes, an operation
//       the agent runs for a client, a compute job a node executes, a resale of tokens
//       inside the system. Four names, one receipt shape, one splitter, one gate.
// What already exists and is NOT restated here:
//   - specs/automation/token-wallet.t27 owns the client side: TRADE_UNITS 3 and its three
//     SHARE_* -- what a client is charged and how that charge is cut. Its rate and its
//     markup are not re-chosen here.
//   - specs/verified/payout.t27 owns the refusals: split_fits and trade_split_fits refuse a
//     split that does not fit, and payout() pays only a credited, verified, referenced
//     receipt. This file CALLS those rules (use verified::payout); it does not copy them.
//   - specs/trinet/settlement_law.t27 (gHashTag/trinity-fpga) owns the mTRI rate for node
//     work, and specs/trinet/node-work-credit.t27 owns what a node receipt must prove
//     before it mints. Neither rate is chosen here.
//   - specs/automation/course-outreach.t27 owns what a message about a course may say and
//     holds every batch to the owner's press. Sending a message is not distributing money;
//     that gate stays exactly where it is (SEND_GATE_UNCHANGED below).
// Why a course fits the same rule: a course is OPEN -- taking it charges the learner
//       nothing (COURSES_OPEN, COURSE_PRICE_TOKENS 0) -- so no receipt is ever raised
//       against a learner. The creator is paid as a CONTRIBUTOR out of the bounty unit of
//       the trade, which is the third share payout.t27 already names for any pool. There is
//       no second economy for courses and no price on a lesson.//       The owner is the first course creator (FIRST_CREATOR). He gets no separate rule: his
//       courses settle by the same functions every other creator's settle by, and no
//       function here reads who the creator is.
// What the creator is paid IN: $TRI (CREATOR_UNIT), the owner's word of 2026-10-23. $TRI has
//       no mainnet and no sale, so TRI_PAYABLE is false and NOTHING leaves today -- the spec
//       records the entitlement and the gate, and does not substitute a dollar token for the
//       coin the owner named, nor claim a payment that cannot happen.
// Why no person in the path (owner, 2026-10-23): accounting and distribution are decided
//       from the receipt and nothing else. A human neither approves, nor blocks, nor raises
//       a payment -- the only door is a receipt that passed the gate. What stays with the
//       owner is outreach: course-outreach's Allow card still gates every message sent in
//       his name, and this file does not touch it.
// Honesty: $TRI is on no mainnet (the site's jetton is on TON testnet), all of it is mined
//       on accepted work with no pre-mine and no sale, and nothing here mints, signs,
//       prices or promises a coin. TRI_VALUE_PROMISED is false and stays false.
// Claim status: DESIGN, no host yet. render's billing still makes one price with MARKUP_PCT
//       and splits nothing (token-wallet v2 note), and no course completion raises a
//       receipt. This must not be sold as live until a host splits a real charge and a real
//       completion has run through these functions.
// v1 (2026-10-23): four services, one receipt gate, courses open with their creators paid as
//       contributors, one owner with no separate rule, no person in the distribution path,
//       three payees of every pool (the provider share is what makes compute join), and the
//       client's side -- the bot free to hold, the client's own tokens and key -- where
//       BYOK_IN_HOST records that the host does not run on a client key yet. The money path
//       end to end: what makes a completion a receipt, and the three conditions (trust model,
//       settlement path, mainnet) under which the coin the creator earns can leave at all.
// v2 (2026-10-23): the books -- the accounting half of the same principle (owner, the same
//       day: "all the accounting ... settled without any person taking part"). A balance is
//       DERIVED from entries; an entry exists only where a receipt passed the gate above and
//       payout() answered PAY_NORMAL; an unreadable book STOPS the run instead of reading as
//       "nothing was owed"; no person writes an entry, and no adjustment entry exists.
// v3 (2026-10-23): ONE DOOR -- settle_service runs the whole chain in one fixed order:
//       what the books cannot read stops the run FIRST (a run that cannot read what was paid
//       must not pay), then the receipt gate, then payout's eligibility, then the books'
//       arithmetic, and only then delivery -- an eligible accrual whose unit cannot leave
//       today is HOLD (earned, not payable), never NONE and never PAY.
// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module automation::service_ledger {

    // The splitter is not reimplemented here: verified::payout owns split_fits,
    // trade_split_fits and payout(), and this module calls them.
    use verified::payout;

    pub const KIND : str = "automation";
    pub const ID : str = "service-ledger";
    pub const REPO : str = "999-multibots-telegraf";
    pub const VERSION : u8 = 3;

    // ---- The services, as one vocabulary -------------------------------------------------
    // One name per service everywhere: in the receipt, in the ledger, in the splitter's log.
    pub const SERVICES : [4]str = ["course", "operation", "node-job", "resale"];
    pub const SERVICE_COUNT : u8 = 4;

    fn service_known(id: str) -> bool {
        if id == "course" { return true; }
        if id == "operation" { return true; }
        if id == "node-job" { return true; }
        if id == "resale" { return true; }
        return false;
    }

    // ---- The one gate ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Money moves from a receipt, once. Four things must hold and none may be assumed:
    // the receipt is RECORDED (never inferred from an attempt), the work it bills was
    // ACCEPTED, a wallet is BOUND to the payee, and no earlier receipt has PAID it.
    // An unknown fact fails the gate; it is never read as "nothing was paid".
    fn may_pay_once(recorded: bool, accepted: bool, wallet_bound: bool, paid_before: bool) -> bool {
        if !recorded { return false; }
        if !accepted { return false; }
        if !wallet_bound { return false; }
        if paid_before { return false; }
        return true;
    }

    // A recorded receipt that cannot be read must stop the run rather than pay from memory:
    // "I do not know what was paid" is never "nothing was paid".
    fn run_distributes(ledger_readable: bool) -> bool {
        return ledger_readable;
    }

    // ---- Courses ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Every course is open: a learner is charged nothing, so a course receipt is raised
    // against a COMPLETION, never against a purchase. The rate a completion earns is an
    // input from the existing economy rules -- this file chooses no amount.
    pub const COURSES_OPEN : bool = true;
    pub const COURSE_PRICE_TOKENS : u32 = 0;
    pub const CREATOR_PAID_AS : str = "contributor";  // payout.t27's third share of a pool
    // The owner's word, 2026-10-23: a course's creator is paid in $TRI. This file records
    // that as the REWARD UNIT and as nothing else -- it mints nothing, prices nothing and
    // promises no value (MINTS_HERE, TRI_VALUE_PROMISED below).
    pub const CREATOR_UNIT : str = "$TRI";
    pub const CREATOR_RATE_SET_HERE : bool = false;   // an input, never chosen in this file
    // $TRI is on no mainnet and has no sale, so the unit cannot be delivered today:
    // TRI_PAYABLE is false, held the way node-work-credit.t27 holds production payout on
    // its own trust model. A qualified completion with an unpayable coin moves NOTHING, and
    // that is reported as "not payable", never as "not earned".
    pub const TRI_PAYABLE : bool = false;

    // The rule above says a creator EARNED; this gate says the unit can be DELIVERED.
    fn creator_paid_now(earned: bool, tri_payable: bool) -> bool {
        return earned && tri_payable;
    }

    // ---- How a course becomes a receipt --------------------------------------------------
    // The course's own numbers (course-outreach.t27 lets a message carry exactly these):
    // 27 lessons, one working widget in each, then a lab of 3. A COMPLETION of a course is
    // the lab passed -- the end of the course, not one lesson in it -- so twenty-seven
    // half-finished starts raise no receipt. What this fn answers is exactly the
    // `completion_recorded` argument course_creator_paid reads.
    pub const COURSE_LESSONS : u8 = 27;
    pub const COURSE_LAB_LESSONS : u8 = 3;
    pub const COMPLETION_IS : str = "lab-passed";
    // DECIDED, not built: no host records completions today (the course pages are static),
    // so today no completion can become a receipt at all.
    pub const COMPLETION_HOST_EXISTS : bool = false;
    // And a completion taken from the learner's own session is the LEARNER's claim until a
    // verifier re-runs it -- the same line specs/trinet/node-work-credit.t27 draws between
    // SELF_REPORTED and VERIFIED records before anything mints.
    pub const COMPLETION_SELF_REPORTED_UNTIL_VERIFIED : bool = true;

    fn completion_receipt(course_known: bool, lab_passed: bool, host_recorded: bool,
                          learner_bound: bool, already_recorded: bool) -> bool {
        if !course_known { return false; }
        if !lab_passed { return false; }
        if !host_recorded { return false; }
        if !learner_bound { return false; }
        if already_recorded { return false; }
        return true;
    }

    // ---- When the coin becomes payable ----------------------------------------------------
    // Three things, and all three: the trust model is agreed (node-work-credit.t27 holds the
    // same one, TRUST_MODEL_AGREED), a live settlement path turns an attested receipt into a
    // mint, and the jetton has a mainnet to live on. The owner declares them; this file
    // measures nothing and flips nothing. All three are false today -- which is why
    // TRI_PAYABLE above is false and why creator_paid_now refuses.
    pub const TRI_TRUST_MODEL_AGREED : bool = false;
    pub const TRI_SETTLEMENT_PATH_LIVE : bool = false;
    pub const TRI_MAINNET_LIVE : bool = false;

    fn tri_payable(trust_agreed: bool, settlement_path_live: bool, mainnet_live: bool) -> bool {
        return trust_agreed && settlement_path_live && mainnet_live;
    }

    // The first course creator of record, on the owner's word of 2026-10-23.
    pub const FIRST_CREATOR : str = "owner";
    // And no rule in this file branches on who the creator is.
    pub const OWNER_HAS_SEPARATE_RULE : bool = false;

    // A creator is paid only from a recorded, verified completion, to a bound wallet, once.
    // The learner is never the payer: if any receipt was raised against a learner, this
    // course rule refuses, because that is not the open course this spec describes.
    fn course_creator_paid(learner_billed: bool, completion_recorded: bool,
                           completion_verified: bool, wallet_bound: bool,
                           paid_before: bool) -> bool {
        if learner_billed { return false; }
        if !completion_recorded { return false; }
        if !completion_verified { return false; }
        if !wallet_bound { return false; }
        if paid_before { return false; }
        return true;
    }

    // ---- Who every pool pays ---------------------------------------------------------------
    // One pool, three payees, for every service above: the executor (the agent that did the
    // work), the provider (the GPU/CPU/FPGA that ran it) and the contributor (whoever brought
    // the work -- for a course, its creator). The names and the refusal are payout.t27's;
    // this file calls them and chooses no rate.
    pub const PAYEES : [3]str = ["executor", "provider", "contributor"];
    pub const PAYEE_COUNT : u8 = 3;
    pub const PROVIDER_RATE_SET_HERE : bool = false;  // an input from settlement_law / catalog

    // Why a GPU, a CPU or a board joins at all: its share comes out of every accepted pool by
    // the same rule, with nobody approving it. The motivation is structural -- being the
    // provider of a service is what entitles the pool's provider share -- not a favor a
    // person grants. WHAT that share is worth follows the settlement law and the catalog
    // cards; both are inputs, and their open questions (WHO_BUYS_TERNARY_COMPUTE) are not
    // papered over here.
    fn pool_has_payees(n: u8) -> bool {
        return n == PAYEE_COUNT;
    }

    // ---- BYOK: the client's side of the same services ---------------------------------------
    // Owner, 2026-10-23: "the bot is free on our side, the user brings his own tokens; we earn
    // on reselling tokens inside the system". So the bot costs nothing to HOLD: no
    // subscription, no card per call. What a client spends is his own token balance at the one
    // rate (token-wallet TOKEN_MICRO_USD), and an operation charges the three units
    // token-wallet v2 already defines. The client's own PROVIDER KEY, when he brings one for
    // the model calls, lives in the request and nowhere else: the host never persists it,
    // never logs it and never reads it between requests -- the same side of that line
    // providers/catalog.t27 site_may_call already draws for the site (the site calls no paid
    // endpoint and holds no key).
    pub const BOT_SUBSCRIPTION_TOKENS : u32 = 0;
    pub const CLIENT_BRINGS_TOKENS : bool = true;
    pub const CLIENT_KEY_STORED : bool = false;
    pub const CLIENT_KEY_LOGGED : bool = false;
    // DECIDED, not in the host: the agent chain today runs on the owner's own keys
    // (agent-provider-chain KIE_ENV_KEY, RESERVE_ENV_KEY). BYOK_IN_HOST flips when a call
    // actually runs on a client-supplied key.
    pub const BYOK_IN_HOST : bool = false;

    // A call may run on the client's key only when he brought one and the host would keep it
    // nowhere: no key in the request is no call, and a route that would persist it is
    // refused -- the key must leave with the request it came in.
    fn byok_may_call(client_key: bool, host_persists: bool) -> bool {
        if !client_key { return false; }
        if host_persists { return false; }
        return true;
    }

    // ---- The books: the accounting half of the same principle ------------------------------
    // Owner, 2026-10-23: "all the accounting ... settled without any person taking part". So
    // a balance is never a number anyone keeps: it is DERIVED from that payee's entries, and
    // an entry exists only where a receipt passed the gate above AND payout() answered
    // PAY_NORMAL for it. No receipt, no entry; no entry, no balance.
    pub const BOOKS_ENTRY_FROM : str = "receipt";
    pub const BALANCE_IS_DERIVED : bool = true;
    pub const HUMAN_WRITES_AN_ENTRY : bool = false;
    pub const ADJUSTMENT_ENTRY_EXISTS : bool = false;
    // DECIDED, not in a host: no service books run anywhere yet. The node network's own books
    // are trinity-fpga's ledger.zig (settle(): spent nonces, slashes) and the host's
    // token-ledger.ts keeps CLIENT token balances, not these accruals -- neither is
    // reimplemented here, and BOOKS_HOST_EXISTS records that these accrual books have no host.
    pub const BOOKS_HOST_EXISTS : bool = false;

    // The books' three answers. The zero byte is STOP on purpose: a fresh or truncated read
    // that says nothing says stop, never "nothing was owed". STOP is not NONE -- an
    // unreadable book both pays nothing and reports that it could not be read.
    pub const BOOK_STOP : u8 = 0;
    pub const BOOK_NONE : u8 = 1;
    pub const BOOK_PAY : u8 = 2;

    // A pool accrues only for a receipt payout() pays normally: credited by the ledger,
    // verified by the engineering verdict, referenced by the settlement record. A slash is
    // the settlement ledger's own decision and books no accrual here; every other refusal
    // books nothing too -- accrual is exactly one outcome wide.
    fn accrues(outcome: u8, verified: bool, verdict_referenced: bool) -> bool {
        return payout(outcome, verified, verdict_referenced) == PAY_NORMAL;
    }

    // Whether `want` may be paid out of an accrued balance. The books are read first (an
    // unreadable book is STOP, never an answer), a paid-above-accrued pair is a broken book
    // and stops too, and a want larger than what is owed pays NOTHING rather than paying
    // part of an untrue balance. Subtracts and never adds, so the outstanding cannot wrap.
    fn books_pay(accrued: u64, paid: u64, want: u64, books_readable: bool) -> u8 {
        if !books_readable { return BOOK_STOP; }
        if paid > accrued { return BOOK_STOP; }
        if want == 0 { return BOOK_NONE; }
        if want > accrued - paid { return BOOK_NONE; }
        return BOOK_PAY;
    }

    // What is left to pay on a consistent pair: accrued minus paid, never negative. The
    // refusal for an inconsistent pair lives in books_pay (BOOK_STOP); this fn computes the
    // view, it never decides a payment.
    fn books_outstanding(accrued: u64, paid: u64) -> u64 {
        if paid > accrued { return 0; }
        return accrued - paid;
    }

    // ---- One door: the whole chain as one call -------------------------------------------
    // The only entry a host needs: every rule above, in one fixed order no caller may
    // rearrange, with a code that says WHICH refusal it was -- so a host reports the reason
    // instead of guessing, and no path into the money exists that skips a rule.
    pub const ONE_DOOR : str = "settle_service";

    // The door's four answers:
    //   STOP  an unknown fact -- the books could not be read, or say more was paid than was
    //         ever accrued. The run stops and pays nothing; STOP is never "nothing owed".
    //   NONE  a rule refused: no receipt, unaccepted work, no wallet, paid before, a learner
    //         billed, payout's refusals, or more than the books say is owed.
    //   HOLD  every rule passed and the books say pay, but the unit cannot leave today
    //         ($TRI on no mainnet): earned and NOT payable -- never reported as not earned.
    //   PAY   pay `want` out of the accrued balance.
    pub const SETTLE_STOP : u8 = 0;
    pub const SETTLE_NONE : u8 = 1;
    pub const SETTLE_HOLD : u8 = 2;
    pub const SETTLE_PAY : u8 = 3;

    fn settle_service(recorded: bool, accepted: bool, wallet_bound: bool, paid_before: bool,
                      learner_billed: bool, books_readable: bool,
                      outcome: u8, verified: bool, verdict_referenced: bool,
                      accrued: u64, paid: u64, want: u64, unit_payable: bool) -> u8 {
        var books_answer : u8 = books_pay(accrued, paid, want, books_readable);
        if books_answer == BOOK_STOP { return SETTLE_STOP; }
        if !may_pay_once(recorded, accepted, wallet_bound, paid_before) { return SETTLE_NONE; }
        if learner_billed { return SETTLE_NONE; }
        if !accrues(outcome, verified, verdict_referenced) { return SETTLE_NONE; }
        if books_answer != BOOK_PAY { return SETTLE_NONE; }
        if !unit_payable { return SETTLE_HOLD; }
        return SETTLE_PAY;
    }

    // ---- No person in the path ------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const HUMAN_APPROVES_PAYMENT : bool = false;
    pub const HUMAN_CAN_BLOCK_PAYMENT : bool = false;
    pub const HUMAN_CAN_RAISE_PAYMENT : bool = false;
    pub const RECEIPT_BEFORE_MONEY : bool = true;
    pub const UNKNOWN_STOPS_THE_RUN : bool = true;
    // The owner's press still gates every MESSAGE about a course; it gates no payment.
    pub const SEND_GATE_UNCHANGED : bool = true;

    // Whether a payment needs a human's press before it leaves. It never does: the receipt
    // decides. An absent press neither blocks a payment that the gate admitted -- that would
    // put the human back in the path -- nor raises one the gate refused.
    fn needs_human_press(receipt_admitted: bool, press_absent: bool) -> bool {
        if receipt_admitted { return false; }
        return press_absent;
    }

    // ---- Honesty ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    pub const TRI_ON_MAINNET : bool = false;
    pub const TRI_SALE_EXISTS : bool = false;   // no pre-mine and no sale (settlement_law)
    pub const MINTS_HERE : bool = false;
    pub const TRI_VALUE_PROMISED : bool = false;
    pub const LIVE : bool = false;              // no host runs this splitter yet

    // Whether a coin may be priced, promised or minted from this file. It never may: the two
    // facts that would have to be true -- a mainnet and a sale -- are both false.
    fn coin_may_be_promised(on_mainnet: bool, sale_exists: bool) -> bool {
        return on_mainnet || sale_exists;
    }

    // ---- Tests -------------------------------------------------------------

    test "one vocabulary, four services, and an unknown name is refused" {
        assert(SERVICE_COUNT == 4);
        assert(service_known("course"));
        assert(service_known("operation"));
        assert(service_known("node-job"));
        assert(service_known("resale"));
        assert(!service_known(""));
        assert(!service_known("consulting"));
    }

    test "money moves only from a recorded accepted receipt to a bound wallet, once" {
        assert(may_pay_once(true, true, true, false));
        assert(!may_pay_once(false, true, true, false));   // an attempt is not a receipt
        assert(!may_pay_once(true, false, true, false));   // rejected work pays nothing
        assert(!may_pay_once(true, true, false, false));   // no bound wallet, no payment
        assert(may_pay_once(true, true, true, true) == false); // idempotent: paid already
    }

    test "an unreadable ledger stops the run instead of paying from memory" {
        assert(run_distributes(true));
        assert(!run_distributes(false));
        assert(UNKNOWN_STOPS_THE_RUN);
    }

    test "every course is open and the learner is never billed" {
        assert(COURSES_OPEN);
        assert(COURSE_PRICE_TOKENS == 0);
        assert(course_creator_paid(false, true, true, true, false));
    }

    test "a billed learner, an unrecorded or unverified completion pays no creator" {
        assert(!course_creator_paid(true, true, true, true, false));
        assert(!course_creator_paid(false, false, true, true, false));
        assert(!course_creator_paid(false, true, false, true, false));
        assert(!course_creator_paid(false, true, true, false, false));
        assert(course_creator_paid(false, true, true, true, true) == false);
    }

    test "a creator earns in $TRI, at a rate this file does not set" {
        assert(CREATOR_PAID_AS == "contributor");
        assert(CREATOR_UNIT == "$TRI");
        assert(!CREATOR_RATE_SET_HERE);
    }

    test "a course completes on its lab of three, recorded once for a bound learner" {
        assert(COURSE_LESSONS == 27);
        assert(COURSE_LAB_LESSONS == 3);
        assert(COMPLETION_IS == "lab-passed");
        assert(completion_receipt(true, true, true, true, false));
        assert(!completion_receipt(false, true, true, true, false));
        assert(!completion_receipt(true, false, true, true, false));
        assert(!completion_receipt(true, true, false, true, false));
        assert(!completion_receipt(true, true, true, false, false));
        assert(completion_receipt(true, true, true, true, true) == false);
    }

    test "no completion host exists yet, and a completion stays a claim until verified" {
        assert(!COMPLETION_HOST_EXISTS);
        assert(COMPLETION_SELF_REPORTED_UNTIL_VERIFIED);
        // the consequence of no host: even a passed lab raises no receipt, because nobody
        // recorded it -- the refusal is the rule's, not a missing fact the rule guesses at
        assert(completion_receipt(true, true, COMPLETION_HOST_EXISTS, true, false) == false);
        assert(completion_receipt(true, true, !COMPLETION_HOST_EXISTS, true, false));
    }

    test "the coin becomes payable only when trust, settlement and mainnet all hold" {
        assert(!TRI_PAYABLE);
        // the flag above and the three conditions say the same thing
        assert(tri_payable(TRI_TRUST_MODEL_AGREED, TRI_SETTLEMENT_PATH_LIVE, TRI_MAINNET_LIVE) == TRI_PAYABLE);
        assert(tri_payable(true, true, true));
        assert(!tri_payable(false, true, true));
        assert(!tri_payable(true, false, true));
        assert(!tri_payable(true, true, false));
        assert(!tri_payable(false, false, false));
    }

    test "an earned completion pays only while the coin is payable, and today it is not" {
        assert(!TRI_PAYABLE);
        assert(creator_paid_now(true, true));
        // earned, but the coin has no mainnet: nothing leaves, and it is "not payable"
        assert(creator_paid_now(true, TRI_PAYABLE) == false);
        assert(creator_paid_now(false, true) == false);
        assert(creator_paid_now(false, TRI_PAYABLE) == false);
    }

    test "the owner created the first course and gets no rule of his own" {
        assert(FIRST_CREATOR == "owner");
        assert(!OWNER_HAS_SEPARATE_RULE);
        // the same functions, whichever creator is named
        assert(course_creator_paid(false, true, true, true, false));
        assert(may_pay_once(true, true, true, false));
    }

    test "one pool pays three, and a provider is one of them" {
        assert(PAYEE_COUNT == 3);
        assert(PAYEES[0] == "executor");
        assert(PAYEES[1] == "provider");
        assert(PAYEES[2] == "contributor");
        assert(pool_has_payees(PAYEE_COUNT));
        assert(pool_has_payees(2) == false);
        assert(!PROVIDER_RATE_SET_HERE);
    }

    test "the bot is free to hold and the client brings his own tokens and key" {
        assert(BOT_SUBSCRIPTION_TOKENS == 0);
        assert(CLIENT_BRINGS_TOKENS);
        assert(!CLIENT_KEY_STORED);
        assert(!CLIENT_KEY_LOGGED);
        assert(byok_may_call(true, false));
        assert(!byok_may_call(false, false));
        assert(!byok_may_call(true, true));
        assert(!byok_may_call(false, true));
    }

    test "BYOK is decided and not yet the host" {
        assert(!BYOK_IN_HOST);
        // the rule exists for the day the host runs it: key brought and not kept, and the
        // other three answers of the same rule
        assert(byok_may_call(true, false));
        assert(!byok_may_call(false, false));
        assert(!byok_may_call(true, true));
        assert(!byok_may_call(false, true));
    }

    test "no person approves, blocks or raises a payment" {
        assert(!HUMAN_APPROVES_PAYMENT);
        assert(!HUMAN_CAN_BLOCK_PAYMENT);
        assert(!HUMAN_CAN_RAISE_PAYMENT);
        assert(RECEIPT_BEFORE_MONEY);
        assert(SEND_GATE_UNCHANGED);
        // an admitted receipt leaves without a press, and an unadmitted one stays without one
        assert(needs_human_press(true, true) == false);
        assert(needs_human_press(true, false) == false);
        assert(needs_human_press(false, true));
        assert(needs_human_press(false, false) == false);
    }

    test "the books grow only from a receipt that payout pays normally" {
        assert(accrues(OUT_CREDITED, true, true));
        assert(!accrues(OUT_CREDITED, false, true));
        assert(!accrues(OUT_CREDITED, true, false));
        assert(!accrues(OUT_NOT_ELIGIBLE, true, true));
        assert(!accrues(OUT_IDENTITY_MISMATCH, true, true));
        assert(!accrues(OUT_CORRUPT_NOT_CHARGED, true, true));
        assert(!accrues(OUT_UNVERIFIABLE_NOT_CHARGED, true, true));
        // a slash is the settlement ledger's own decision: it books no accrual here
        assert(!accrues(OUT_REJECTED_AND_SLASHED, true, true));
        assert(!accrues(255, true, true));
        assert(BOOKS_ENTRY_FROM == "receipt");
    }

    test "an unreadable book stops the run instead of reading as nothing owed" {
        assert(books_pay(10, 0, 5, false) == BOOK_STOP);
        // the zero byte of a fresh or truncated read says stop, never "nothing was owed"
        assert(BOOK_STOP == 0);
        // paid more than was accrued: a broken book, not an answer
        assert(books_pay(10, 11, 1, true) == BOOK_STOP);
        assert(books_pay(10, 0, 5, true) == BOOK_PAY);
        assert(books_pay(10, 5, 5, true) == BOOK_PAY);    // exactly what is owed
        assert(books_pay(10, 0, 11, true) == BOOK_NONE);  // more than is owed pays nothing
        assert(books_pay(10, 10, 1, true) == BOOK_NONE);  // already paid in full
        assert(books_pay(10, 0, 0, true) == BOOK_NONE);   // nothing asked
    }

    test "no balance is hand-set and no adjustment entry exists" {
        assert(BALANCE_IS_DERIVED);
        assert(!HUMAN_WRITES_AN_ENTRY);
        assert(!ADJUSTMENT_ENTRY_EXISTS);
        assert(!BOOKS_HOST_EXISTS);
        assert(books_outstanding(30, 12) == 18);
        assert(books_outstanding(0, 0) == 0);
        // an overpaid pair reads as a broken book (BOOK_STOP above), never as a negative sum
        assert(books_outstanding(12, 30) == 0);
    }

    test "what is accrued is exactly what is paid plus what is owed" {
        assert(12 + books_outstanding(30, 12) == 30);
        assert(0 + books_outstanding(30, 0) == 30);
        assert(30 + books_outstanding(30, 30) == 30);
        assert(books_pay(30, 31, 1, true) == BOOK_STOP);
        // and accrual never exceeds the pool: the splitter's refusal is the conservation rule
        assert(split_fits(10, 6, 3, 1));
        assert(!split_fits(10, 6, 3, 2));
    }

    test "one door runs the whole chain and pays only when every rule said yes" {
        assert(ONE_DOOR == "settle_service");
        // the full path: recorded, accepted, bound wallet, paid once, no learner billed,
        // readable books, a credited verified referenced receipt, books that say pay, and a
        // unit that can leave today
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_PAY);
        // and a want beyond the outstanding is refused by the books, not paid partially
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 10, 1, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        // earned but the unit cannot leave: HOLD -- "not payable", never "not earned"
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, false) == SETTLE_HOLD);
        // the same answer through the real gate: today $TRI is unpayable, so the door holds
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5,
                              tri_payable(TRI_TRUST_MODEL_AGREED, TRI_SETTLEMENT_PATH_LIVE,
                                          TRI_MAINNET_LIVE)) == SETTLE_HOLD);
        assert(creator_paid_now(true, TRI_PAYABLE) == false);
        // HOLD only when the books already said pay: nothing owed with an unpayable coin is
        // NONE, not a hold over an empty balance
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 10, 0, false) == SETTLE_NONE);
    }

    test "the door stops on what it cannot read and names each refusal in order" {
        // unreadable books stop the run BEFORE the gate -- paid_before cannot be judged
        // without knowing what was paid
        assert(settle_service(false, false, false, true, true, false,
                              OUT_NOT_ELIGIBLE, false, false, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_STOP);
        // overpaid books are broken books: stop, never a negative balance
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 11, 1, true) == SETTLE_STOP);
        // the gate, one refusal at a time
        assert(settle_service(false, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        assert(settle_service(true, false, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        assert(settle_service(true, true, false, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, true, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, true, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        // payout's refusals reach the door unchanged
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, false, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, false, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_IDENTITY_MISMATCH, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        // a slash is the settlement ledger's own decision: it pays nothing through this door
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_REJECTED_AND_SLASHED, true, true, 10, 0, 5, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
        // and more than is owed pays nothing at all
        assert(settle_service(true, true, true, false, false, true,
                              OUT_CREDITED, true, true, 10, 0, 11, true) == SETTLE_NONE);
    }

    test "the splitter refuses a split that does not fit the pool, by calling payout" {
        // verified::payout's own refusals, reached here without restating their arithmetic
        assert(split_fits(10, 6, 3, 1) == true);
        assert(split_fits(10, 6, 3, 2) == false);
        assert(trade_split_fits(24, 8, 8, 8) == true);
        assert(trade_split_fits(24, 8, 8, 9) == false);
        // and payout pays only a credited, verified, referenced receipt
        assert(payout(OUT_CREDITED, true, true) == PAY_NORMAL);
        assert(payout(OUT_CREDITED, false, true) == PAY_NONE);
        assert(payout(OUT_NOT_ELIGIBLE, true, true) == PAY_NONE);
    }

    test "no coin is promised, sold or minted by this file" {
        assert(!TRI_ON_MAINNET);
        assert(!TRI_SALE_EXISTS);
        assert(!MINTS_HERE);
        assert(!TRI_VALUE_PROMISED);
        assert(!LIVE);
        assert(coin_may_be_promised(TRI_ON_MAINNET, TRI_SALE_EXISTS) == false);
        assert(coin_may_be_promised(true, false));
        assert(coin_may_be_promised(false, true));
    }

    invariant the_learner_is_never_billed {
        assert COURSES_OPEN == true;
        assert COURSE_PRICE_TOKENS == 0;
    }

    invariant the_books_are_written_from_receipts_alone {
        assert BOOKS_ENTRY_FROM == "receipt";
        assert BALANCE_IS_DERIVED == true;
        assert HUMAN_WRITES_AN_ENTRY == false;
        assert ADJUSTMENT_ENTRY_EXISTS == false;
    }

    test "VERSION says what the header's last note says" {
        assert(VERSION == 3);
        assert(VERSION as u32 == SERVICE_COUNT - 1);
        assert(may_pay_once(true, true, true, false));
    }
}

// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY
